# Testing & quality engineering anchor

Apply when creating or changing tests, test infrastructure, quality gates, regression coverage, benchmarks, fuzz/property tests, or CI verification.

## Hard invariants

- Test behavior and invariants, not implementation trivia.
- Every reproducible bug fix should gain a regression test where practical.
- Prefer deterministic synchronization over sleeps and timing luck.
- PostgreSQL-specific behavior requires real PostgreSQL tests.
- Flaky tests are defects; retry-until-green is not a fix.
- Coverage is diagnostic evidence, not proof of correctness.
- Use the lowest layer that reliably proves the behavior.
- Quality gates must remain actionable and reproducible locally.

